<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Runde lighthouse and bird-cliff loop — Goksøyr, Lundeura, Rundebranden and Runde lighthouse full loop [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>From Goksøyr parking on Runde, climb to the plateau, visit Lundeura and Rundebranden, continue along the western cliff and descend to the lower lighthouse courtyard. Return on eastern paths and the northern boardwalk. Plan roughly 8.5 km and 3.5 hours plus stops; climbing figures are approximate. Dry, snow-free September is recommended. From 15 March through 31 August, use the full circuit only if current official instructions explicitly permit every required protected leg; the marked-viewpoint exception is not established for this whole route. Obey year-round signs and closures, protect birds and stay back from unprotected cliffs. Expect slippery ground, steep descents and road traffic. Private lighthouse buildings and accommodation are excluded.

Route geometry: © OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0 — https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright; https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/. Source: https://www.openstreetmap.org/api/0.6/map?bbox=5.56,62.385,5.64,62.435. Changes: directed original-node slices from 27 complete captured walking ways form 41 legs; only duplicate shared junction nodes removed. Canonical display is simplified using existing source vertices. No synthetic connectors, private guide-track coordinates, viewpoint snaps or elevations. Descriptive two-dimensional planning geometry, not navigation-grade or permission.

